  ;; =====================================================================
  ;; Important Design Notes
  ;; =====================================================================

  (text "DESIGN NOTES:\n\n1. STM32F407VGT6 handles ALL sensor acquisition and local processing\n2. ESP32-S3 handles cloud connectivity ONLY (WiFi, BLE, MQTT, HTTP)\n3. STM32 sends processed readings to ESP32 via USART3 bridge\n4. RS485 Modbus runs on STM32 USART2 via MAX3485 transceiver\n5. Both MCUs share 3.3V power rail from TPS63020\n6. IWDG on STM32 provides 4-second watchdog protection\n7. DIP switch on PE0/PE1 selects operating mode at boot\n8. All external I/O protected with TVS diodes\n\nRS485 BUS WIRING:\n  - Use twisted pair cable (Cat5e or dedicated RS485 cable)\n  - 120Ω termination at each end of bus\n  - Maximum bus length: 1200m at 9600 baud\n  - Maximum 32 devices on bus\n  - Shield connected to GND at one end only\n\nJ16 PINOUT (Phoenix Contact MC series):\n  Pin 1 = A (non-inverting, D+)\n  Pin 2 = B (inverting, D-)\n  Pin 3 = GND (signal ground)\n  Pin 4 = Shield (chassis ground)"
    (at 55.88 240 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left))
  )

